    "Waiting for a newly inserted Places folder before opening a closed lazy menu was an invalid test precondition, even if the view had been populated earlier. The final check prepares it through actual native opening.",
    "A retained nested bookmark run received an explicit expired-ID rejection while closing its parent. Twelve controlled protocol cases verify bounded recovery only for definite non-delivery; the final live browser check has no unhandled callback errors.",
    "The old provider failed the physical root identity negative control, changing its compositor window ID from 2 to 3. Retaining the native root fixes this without browser/model-side menu geometry.",
    "One lifecycle image captured the root before its lazy popup buffer mapped. The raw eager/prepared images are retained; the corrected mapping barrier passes full unaltered pixel equality.",
    "The first final Firefox environment collector referenced a nonexistent 03 adapter filename; the unchanged adapter remains the 02 build. It was corrected after the owner-loss test, so final hashes are current but sandbox process evidence comes from the matching 02 adapter cohort.",
    "The first Chromium cleanup audit incorrectly treated a PID-namespace log ID of 1 as a guest PID. The corrected audit uses the recorded guest process tree; no process was killed on the basis of that log ID."
